Any who, sorry that that happened.

00:15:53.320 --> 00:15:54.600
That's pretty devastating.

00:15:54.600 --> 00:15:58.480
I would just say that usually capital problems are,

00:16:01.680 --> 00:16:03.200
what I've learned from you, Evan,

00:16:03.200 --> 00:16:05.480
is that when you are talking about capital problems,

00:16:05.480 --> 00:16:08.400
you're talking about also a value.

00:16:08.400 --> 00:16:10.280
Like if you need more capital,

00:16:10.280 --> 00:16:13.080
you have to start thinking about your value,

00:16:13.080 --> 00:16:14.440
what value are you providing?

00:16:14.440 --> 00:16:18.640
And so if you really can provide great value,

00:16:18.640 --> 00:16:22.760
you will start to see that change in capital.

00:16:24.360 --> 00:16:28.160
And he talks about asking for help from Oprah

00:16:28.160 --> 00:16:29.960
or some kind of sponsorship.

00:16:29.960 --> 00:16:32.900
And another thing that I hear you talk a lot about

00:16:33.300 --> 00:16:35.300
is just in general,

00:16:35.300 --> 00:16:40.300
don't go into looking for investors right away.

00:16:40.460 --> 00:16:42.780
Like you got to bootstrap it in the beginning

00:16:42.780 --> 00:16:45.380
and really just, well, in this case,

00:16:45.380 --> 00:16:47.500
it looks like it's, I don't even know if it's his business

00:16:47.500 --> 00:16:52.220
or someone else's business, but he's in general electronics.

00:16:52.220 --> 00:16:55.940
So yeah, I don't think that would be the way to go

00:16:56.820 --> 00:16:59.500
necessarily looking for some celebrity

00:16:59.500 --> 00:17:04.500
