00:17:08.820 --> 00:17:10.880
and differentiating your business

00:17:10.880 --> 00:17:13.680
from other general electronics in some way.

00:17:13.680 --> 00:17:18.680
And so sorry, I hope that you can get to the next level.

00:17:22.040 --> 00:17:26.180
Yeah, definitely sad.

00:17:26.180 --> 00:17:28.660
I would start with not having so much

00:17:28.660 --> 00:17:32.620
of your personal value tied up in your business.

00:17:34.340 --> 00:17:37.060
You feel like you're dead because your business,

00:17:37.060 --> 00:17:38.940
something negative happened in your business.

00:17:38.940 --> 00:17:42.220
There's a lot more to life than just the company doing.

00:17:42.220 --> 00:17:44.540
And I get that it's super important.

00:17:44.540 --> 00:17:46.780
Your life is super, your business is super important.

00:17:46.780 --> 00:17:51.100
I would be sad if my YouTube channel disappeared

00:17:51.100 --> 00:17:52.460
or whatever I was working on,

00:17:52.460 --> 00:17:55.260
my book manuscript blew up or whatever.

00:17:56.260 --> 00:17:59.140
But not to the point where I'm giving up on life.

00:18:00.580 --> 00:18:02.340
And it may just mean also kind of,

00:18:03.700 --> 00:18:06.300
oh, this guy's stealing my red or my blue.

00:18:06.300 --> 00:18:08.180
Ah, unbelievable that guy.

00:18:10.580 --> 00:18:13.180
It may be trying to figure out what value you can add

00:18:14.300 --> 00:18:17.540
and being grateful for your life beyond just your business

00:18:17.540 --> 00:18:20.040
and not having everything so tied up in it.

00:18:21.140 --> 00:18:24.100
That being said, the most immediate thing I would look at

00:18:24.140 --> 00:18:28.940
is how can you get insurance for what you're doing?

00:18:28.940 --> 00:18:30.860
It sounds like a classic insurance case

00:18:30.860 --> 00:18:34.140
where something gets stolen, something gets lost.

00:18:34.140 --> 00:18:35.940
To prevent something happening again,

00:18:37.140 --> 00:18:40.180
look at some insurance products that don't know,

00:18:40.180 --> 00:18:41.460
there's gotta be some that exist

00:18:41.460 --> 00:18:43.160
for what you're trying to do.

00:18:44.220 --> 00:18:45.780
That doesn't help with the immediate solution,

00:18:45.780 --> 00:18:49.220
but it helps with things in the future

00:18:49.220 --> 00:18:51.060
to prevent that from happening again.

00:18:54.740 --> 00:18:57.020
Nobody's coming to save you, right?

00:18:57.020 --> 00:18:58.540
This is tough love time.

00:18:58.540 --> 00:19:00.220
Nobody's coming to save you.

00:19:00.220 --> 00:19:03.540
Bad stuff happens and you gotta figure it out.

00:19:03.540 --> 00:19:07.400
Oprah is not gonna write you a check to save your business.

00:19:07.400 --> 00:19:09.280
You have to save you.

00:19:09.280 --> 00:19:10.540
And you have to take responsibility

00:19:10.540 --> 00:19:11.720
for where you're at right now.

00:19:11.720 --> 00:19:13.540
And yeah, bad stuff happens.

00:19:13.540 --> 00:19:16.240
Things burn down, stuff gets stolen.

00:19:16.240 --> 00:19:18.780
You get back up and you keep going.

00:19:18.780 --> 00:19:22.300
That's the life of an entrepreneur, unfortunately.

00:19:22.300 --> 00:19:23.580
It's not about your resources,

00:19:23.980 --> 00:19:25.060
it's about your resourcefulness.

00:19:25.060 --> 00:19:30.060
And seeing Oprah do something amazing to help people out

00:19:30.140 --> 00:19:31.660
and think that that's my,

00:19:31.660 --> 00:19:34.620
if that's your plan to save your business

00:19:34.620 --> 00:19:37.720
that Oprah has to come in and give you a check,

00:19:37.720 --> 00:19:40.240
you are gonna be struggling for a long time.

00:19:42.820 --> 00:19:44.740
Wow, it's real.

00:19:44.740 --> 00:19:45.820
Yeah, it's real.

00:19:45.820 --> 00:19:50.420
But Oprah doesn't care about your shipping business.

00:19:50.420 --> 00:19:52.180
Nobody's gonna care about your shipping business

00:19:52.180 --> 00:19:53.120
as much as you do.

00:19:54.140 --> 00:19:57.240
So you have to go out and save your business yourself.

00:19:58.460 --> 00:20:00.860
And just in general, I get a lot of people saying,

00:20:00.860 --> 00:20:02.760
hey, can you, I'm really struggling,

00:20:02.760 --> 00:20:06.500
can you give me $500 or $10,000 or $100,000

00:20:06.500 --> 00:20:08.180
or whatever it is.

00:20:08.180 --> 00:20:11.380
Like that's not how it's gonna work for anybody.

00:20:11.380 --> 00:20:14.020
And most people, you send something to Oprah,

00:20:14.020 --> 00:20:15.380
she's just gonna ignore you.

00:20:16.380 --> 00:20:18.460
Right, I'm, this may be harsh,

00:20:18.460 --> 00:20:20.460
but at least it's the real talk.

00:20:20.460 --> 00:20:22.540
I'd like to think that she wouldn't ignore me

00:20:22.540 --> 00:20:25.040
if I sent her a letter.

00:20:25.040 --> 00:20:26.180
Yeah, but she will.

00:20:26.180 --> 00:20:30.580
Like, you know, look at how many people send Oprah stuff.

00:20:31.720 --> 00:20:32.560
Right?

00:20:33.400 --> 00:20:34.240
It's just.

00:20:34.240 --> 00:20:36.380
At least you don't ignore her.

00:20:36.380 --> 00:20:39.700
She can't keep up, right?

00:20:39.700 --> 00:20:41.460
Like a plan like that. You're right, you're right.

00:20:41.460 --> 00:20:43.700
It's just, so it's on you.

00:20:43.700 --> 00:20:45.780
And then back to your point, like, no, okay,

00:20:45.780 --> 00:20:48.180
tactical, how do you actually get out of this?

00:20:50.380 --> 00:20:52.420
It's to your point about adding more value

00:20:53.260 --> 00:20:54.080
from before, right?

00:20:54.080 --> 00:20:55.220
What can you do to bring value

00:20:55.220 --> 00:20:58.340
so that you're not just another wholesaler

00:20:58.340 --> 00:20:59.620
of electronics equipment,

00:20:59.620 --> 00:21:01.540
but there's something special, unique,

00:21:01.540 --> 00:21:04.820
and different about you so that you can make more money.

00:21:06.420 --> 00:21:09.260
And you just gotta get through this period.

00:21:09.260 --> 00:21:12.140
Like, I don't see an investor coming in

00:21:12.140 --> 00:21:15.460
and giving you money to save your business right now.

00:21:16.340 --> 00:21:17.600
Yeah, yeah.

00:21:17.600 --> 00:21:20.940
And that sucks, and that may mean bootstrapping, right?

00:21:21.300 --> 00:21:25.240
If I lost all my money, and I lost my YouTube channel,

00:21:25.240 --> 00:21:27.180
and I lost everything that I was doing,

00:21:29.460 --> 00:21:31.420
I would start up on YouTube again.

00:21:32.500 --> 00:21:35.180
And I would do it all myself.

00:21:35.180 --> 00:21:36.920
And I'd go back to one video a week.

00:21:36.920 --> 00:21:41.920
And that would be a huge ego pill to swallow.

00:21:41.940 --> 00:21:43.660
And that's really the test of like,

00:21:43.660 --> 00:21:44.640
do you love what you're doing?

00:21:44.640 --> 00:21:47.380
Now you're providing some real value, right?

00:21:47.380 --> 00:21:49.340
I would go back to doing one video a week,

00:21:49.380 --> 00:21:53.020
doing everything myself, and that's it.

00:21:53.020 --> 00:21:56.560
So you might have to scale back a little bit.

00:21:58.060 --> 00:21:59.940
Oh, people are upset that they have no jungle.

00:21:59.940 --> 00:22:02.440
Yeah, sorry guys, I'm not really paying attention.

00:22:04.180 --> 00:22:06.020
I'm trying to answer questions.

00:22:06.020 --> 00:22:08.420
I'm being a bad teammate at the moment.

00:22:10.140 --> 00:22:12.140
But hopefully helping some listeners.

00:22:12.140 --> 00:22:15.900
I don't think you could ever go back to one video a week.

00:22:15.900 --> 00:22:18.820
Well, I'm saying like, if I lost everything, right?

00:22:19.100 --> 00:22:22.300
This guy had some really bad luck, right?

00:22:24.640 --> 00:22:26.380
Something happened, he lost his container.

00:22:26.380 --> 00:22:30.340
Maybe he put his life savings into that container, right?

00:22:30.340 --> 00:22:33.620
So the equivalent, if I lost everything I had,

00:22:33.620 --> 00:22:35.460
I lost my channel and lost my team

00:22:35.460 --> 00:22:37.620
and couldn't afford to pay anybody or whatever,

00:22:37.620 --> 00:22:41.620
I would start up again, just smaller,

00:22:41.620 --> 00:22:42.860
and then build back up.

00:22:45.340 --> 00:22:47.700
So that's what he has to do.

00:22:47.980 --> 00:22:49.140
Just do it smarter.

00:22:49.140 --> 00:22:51.300
Don't count on somebody coming to save you.

00:22:51.300 --> 00:22:53.780
Take out insurance next time so that you're not screwed over

00:22:53.780 --> 00:22:55.260
if something does happen.

00:22:55.260 --> 00:22:58.380
And to make more money, provide more value

00:22:58.380 --> 00:23:00.260
in what you're selling to differentiate yourself

00:23:00.260 --> 00:23:02.820
so it's not just another guy selling the same stuff.

00:23:06.900 --> 00:23:07.780
That's it.

00:23:07.780 --> 00:23:08.620
Great.

00:23:11.340 --> 00:23:12.180
You ready?

00:23:12.180 --> 00:23:13.000
Yeah, I'm ready.

00:23:13.000 --> 00:23:14.900
Hopefully the next one, I mean,

00:23:14.940 --> 00:23:18.140
I feel like it's maybe a little bit tough love there,

00:23:18.140 --> 00:23:19.620
but it's true.

00:23:20.580 --> 00:23:22.300
So let's see, let's see how it goes with the next one.

00:23:22.300 --> 00:23:23.300
Let's turn it around.

00:23:27.300 --> 00:23:31.060
Okay, we got a question from Adam,

00:23:31.060 --> 00:23:36.060
and he says he had gotten below average SAT scores

00:23:37.060 --> 00:23:39.760
and rejected from every college he applied to.

00:23:41.580 --> 00:23:43.820
Then he started his first real semester

00:23:43.820 --> 00:23:45.220
at a community college.

00:23:45.220 --> 00:23:48.300
He was super driven and motivated in all his classes

00:23:48.300 --> 00:23:51.380
and then finally got accepted.

00:23:51.380 --> 00:23:53.140
So he did so well in the community college

00:23:53.140 --> 00:23:56.300
that he then got accepted and was able to transfer

00:23:56.300 --> 00:23:57.900
to the university of his dreams.

00:23:58.980 --> 00:24:02.260
And anyway, to his surprise,

00:24:02.260 --> 00:24:05.420
he got to the new university of his dreams

00:24:05.420 --> 00:24:08.640
and now he doesn't feel driven

00:24:08.640 --> 00:24:11.620
and he's not as excited about his classes

00:24:11.660 --> 00:24:14.160
like he was in the community college

00:24:14.160 --> 00:24:16.140
and he feels really isolated.

00:24:16.140 --> 00:24:19.500
So he's starting to wonder why he's there at all

00:24:19.500 --> 00:24:21.500
and he's asking just for general advice.

00:24:23.540 --> 00:24:28.540
So I guess I would say first and foremost,

00:24:30.980 --> 00:24:34.060
what comes to mind is, you know,

00:24:34.060 --> 00:24:37.980
I always lose my motivation and my drive

00:24:37.980 --> 00:24:42.980
when I lose my why and when I lose my vision.

00:24:44.980 --> 00:24:47.720
And so we can all relate.

00:24:47.720 --> 00:24:49.500
I know we can all relate to times

00:24:49.500 --> 00:24:51.860
when like we are way more driven than others.

00:24:53.060 --> 00:24:55.980
And I don't necessarily think it means

00:24:55.980 --> 00:24:59.280
that the school that he's at now isn't the right place

00:24:59.280 --> 00:25:01.500
because I think if you have a really good strong why

00:25:01.500 --> 00:25:05.020
and vision for what it is that you wanna do,

00:25:05.020 --> 00:25:08.020
then you find the motivation kind of wherever you are.

00:25:10.220 --> 00:25:13.260
But it sounds obviously like his why is unclear.

00:25:13.260 --> 00:25:15.820
My question to you, Adam, would be,

00:25:15.820 --> 00:25:19.320
can you figure out what it was about the,

00:25:21.240 --> 00:25:24.580
what was different in the community college?

00:25:24.580 --> 00:25:28.380
What was really clear to you about what you were doing there

00:25:28.380 --> 00:25:30.700
that gave you motivation and inspiration

00:25:30.700 --> 00:25:32.960
to be really driven?

00:25:32.960 --> 00:25:36.320
Because I think if he can figure that out,

00:25:36.320 --> 00:25:40.960
he can bring that to the new university.

00:25:43.720 --> 00:25:45.400
Yeah, that's all I got.

00:25:45.400 --> 00:25:48.720
All right, we just got a kill, so super happy about that.

00:25:48.720 --> 00:25:49.560
Pretty exciting.

00:25:53.040 --> 00:25:53.960
Adam, right?

00:25:55.200 --> 00:25:56.300
Yes, Adam.

00:25:56.300 --> 00:26:01.300
Adam, I think it's okay to realize that you change

00:26:01.860 --> 00:26:05.380
and what you think you like, sometimes you don't like.

00:26:06.660 --> 00:26:09.480
You get into a relationship with a girl

00:26:09.480 --> 00:26:10.940
and you think it's gonna be great

00:26:10.940 --> 00:26:14.380
and then once you start in, it's not great.

00:26:16.900 --> 00:26:19.500
You start a business and it's not working

00:26:19.500 --> 00:26:22.560
or you start a business and you realize

00:26:22.560 --> 00:26:24.660
you don't love this thing anymore.

00:26:24.660 --> 00:26:26.340
And what most people do is stick with it.

00:26:26.340 --> 00:26:29.200
What most people do is they stay in the same job

00:26:29.200 --> 00:26:30.840
because maybe they were good at it

00:26:31.320 --> 00:26:33.880
or because their parents wanted them to do it or whatever

00:26:33.880 --> 00:26:36.040
and they just wake up and drive to a job

00:26:36.040 --> 00:26:37.840
that they hate every day.

00:26:37.840 --> 00:26:39.600
Where the best thing to do is explore

00:26:39.600 --> 00:26:41.900
until you find the thing that makes you come alive

00:26:41.900 --> 00:26:46.180
and do that until it doesn't make you come alive anymore.

00:26:48.840 --> 00:26:51.400
You have genius level talent at something

00:26:52.520 --> 00:26:54.240
and you have to find what that is.

00:26:55.500 --> 00:26:58.120
And that comes by exploring.

00:26:58.120 --> 00:26:59.420
And if you keep doing things,

00:26:59.540 --> 00:27:02.860
if you stay here doing something that you don't love,

00:27:02.860 --> 00:27:06.340
you're never gonna be the best version of you.

00:27:06.340 --> 00:27:08.560
So that may mean switching majors.

00:27:08.560 --> 00:27:11.840
Maybe you wanna go try something else

00:27:11.840 --> 00:27:14.600
but staying within your university.

00:27:15.980 --> 00:27:20.980
That may mean dropping out and going to do something else.

00:27:22.500 --> 00:27:24.180
You look at Steve Jobs as an example

00:27:24.180 --> 00:27:25.820
and he dropped out of his school

00:27:25.820 --> 00:27:27.180
where everybody thought he was crazy.

00:27:27.180 --> 00:27:29.500
To go back to school as a volunteer,

00:27:29.500 --> 00:27:31.180
like not get credit,

00:27:31.180 --> 00:27:32.780
to learn about fonts and calligraphy

00:27:32.780 --> 00:27:34.860
and that helped him create.

00:27:34.860 --> 00:27:38.180
